<section class="section section--page">
  <div class="wrap stack">
    <h2 class="m0">For churches without bells</h2>
    <p class="section-p">A church without a tower can still ring. An electronic carillon brings the sound of cast bronze bells through speakers set in a steeple or on an exterior wall, with nothing to cast, nothing to build, and no structure to reinforce. It rings the Call to Worship and the Angelus, peals for weddings, tolls for funerals, and keeps Westminster chimes with the hour. Its library holds thousands of hymns, Ave Maria and Gregorian chant among them. A grant can cover one.</p>
  </div>
</section>

{#- How a grant works and what to send (client, 2026-09-29): proposal first, no inquiry step,
    no reply step, no "approve", no invitation to write and ask. Up to 80 percent, never all.
