<section class="section section--page">
  <div class="wrap stack">
    <h2 class="m0">How a grant works</h2>
    <p class="section-p">The funds are in place. A grant covers up to 80 percent of a project's cost, never all of it. A parish that has put something of its own into its bells or organ will look after them, so every applicant carries a share.</p>
    <p class="section-p">There is no fixed amount. Every grant is set case by case, from the proposal in front of us and the funds we have available.</p>
    <p class="section-p">We like to see the parish and the wider community involved: a congregation behind the project, volunteers, local giving, a town that wants to hear its bells again.</p>
    <p class="section-p">Bell and organ work often runs in phases over several years as funds allow. Tell us your timeline, and a grant can be shaped to fit it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--page">
  <div class="wrap stack">
    <h2 class="m0">What to send</h2>
    <p class="section-p">Come with a proposal in hand. Talk to the bell foundry, organ builder, or glass studio first and get their quote. That is the groundwork, and we start from it. A complete submission has five parts:</p>
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li><i class="ph ph-check icon icon--sm icon--brass" aria-hidden="true"></i>The quote or proposal from the maker you intend to use</li>
      <li><i class="ph ph-check icon icon--sm icon--brass" aria-hidden="true"></i>The project's timeline, with any phases</li>
      <li><i class="ph ph-check icon icon--sm icon--brass" aria-hidden="true"></i>Photographs of the bells, organ, or windows as they are now</li>
      <li><i class="ph ph-check icon icon--sm icon--brass" aria-hidden="true"></i>The total cost, and the share you are asking us to cover</li>
      <li><i class="ph ph-check icon icon--sm icon--brass" aria-hidden="true"></i>A note on how the parish and community are involved</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="section-p">Everything is submitted online through the form at the end of the Resources page, with the proposal and photographs attached. There is nothing to print and nothing to mail.</p>
  </div>
</section>
